   * Register a new administrator account with email and password credentials. This operation creates a new administrator record in the discussion_board_administrators table with the provided email, hashed password, and optional display name and bio. The email must be unique across all administrator accounts as enforced by the unique constraint on the email column. Upon successful registration, the administrator is assigned a 'regular' grade by default and can immediately log in to access administrative features.
   *
   * The password is hashed using a secure algorithm before storage in the password_hash column. The created_at and updated_at timestamps are automatically set to record the account creation time. The administrator starts with no active sessions until they log in.
   *
   * This operation is public and does not require authentication, allowing new administrators to register themselves. After registration, the administrator should use the login operation to obtain JWT tokens for authenticated access to protected resources.
   *
   * @setHeader token.access Authorization
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Administrator registration credentials including email, password, and optional profile information
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type join
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor administrator
   * @x-autobe-specification Create a new record in discussion_board_administrators table with email, password_hash (hashed), display_name, bio, grade='regular', created_at, and updated_at fields. Validate email uniqueness before insertion. Hash the password using bcrypt or similar secure algorithm. Return authorization tokens (access and refresh) in the response. Set authorizationType to 'join' for proper authentication handling.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post("join")
  public async join(
    @Ip()
    ip: string,
    @TypedBody()
    body: IDiscussionBoardAdministrator.IJoin,
  ): Promise<IDiscussionBoardAdministrator.IAuthorized> {
    try {
      return await postDiscussionBoardAuthAdministratorJoin({
        ip,
        body,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Authenticate an administrator with email and password credentials. This operation validates the provided credentials against the discussion_board_administrators table by comparing the hashed password with the stored password_hash. Upon successful authentication, a new session record is created in the discussion_board_administrator_sessions table with access and refresh token hashes.
   *
   * The session includes connection metadata (IP address, href, referrer) for security auditing. The access token expires after 15 minutes and the refresh token expires after 7 days, as configured in the access_token_expires_at and refresh_token_expires_at fields. Only one active session is allowed per administrator, enforced by the unique constraint on discussion_board_administrator_id.
   *
   * This operation is public and does not require prior authentication. The returned tokens enable the administrator to access protected administrative resources and manage content, users, and system settings.
   *
   * @setHeader token.access Authorization
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Administrator login credentials including email and password
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type login
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor administrator
   * @x-autobe-specification Validate email and password against discussion_board_administrators table. Hash the provided password and compare with stored password_hash. If valid, create or update a session record in discussion_board_administrator_sessions with token hashes, connection metadata, and expiration timestamps. Return JWT tokens (access and refresh) in the response. Set authorizationType to 'login' for proper authentication handling.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post("login")
  public async login(
    @Ip()
    ip: string,
    @TypedBody()
    body: IDiscussionBoardAdministrator.ILogin,
  ): Promise<IDiscussionBoardAdministrator.IAuthorized> {
